## Project origin

Concord originated from the Code With Antonio "Google Docs Clone"
tutorial (a commercial Next.js/Clerk/Convex/Liveblocks course product).
The project was deliberately rebuilt into an original engineering work:
the synchronization stack — the C++20/WASM sequence CRDT, the Rust sync
gateways, the binary wire protocol, the PostgreSQL durable plane
(schema, ingest, snapshots, recovery, history), and the browser
local-first runtime — is original to this repository. The pristine
tutorial baseline is preserved for transparency at the git tag
`antonio-original-baseline`.

The baseline-derived material is resolved as documented in
`docs/PROVENANCE.md`: all baseline artwork, fonts, favicon, template
copy, and the tutorial-identical source files were replaced with
original Concord implementations during the hardening pass; the
remaining baseline-derived editor chrome was rewritten. A CI gate
(`scripts/security/provenance-check.sh`) fails if any shipped file is
byte-identical to the baseline without an explicit, verified,
permissively-licensed allowlist entry.

